"85a05273-d7c5-5a81-9a38-af7c6efc1cfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-7643" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{3}{4} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+12 & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =0,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74a508c1-2379-590f-85f5-386a1990f137"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9457"] :question/problem "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{4}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{2}{3} & =1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+2 & =3 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =-5,\\,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(-3,0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039005/assets/f491b886477531fbd081cbdd73244e9cf489bd2474528ea27b66b187b9eb170e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-1/35638cd106a0744b29c569474626837e9a8855d79c5c7831a13c2137a3fe6edc" :answer/id #uuid "91fcaded-11a6-5d75-93a2-c82926af1fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5-\\sqrt{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1be17426-dedb-5659-8abd-74cac156ddf0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274480/field-1/35638cd106a0744b29c569474626837e9a8855d79c5c7831a13c2137a3fe6edc" :answer-field/choices ["q-274480/field-1/35638cd106a0744b29c569474626837e9a8855d79c5c7831a13c2137a3fe6edc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "eef22395-cf70-585c-b636-9b76eb7bcf15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2082b768-07b8-5fe8-9073-662787509de8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274480/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-274480/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-3/70a2076757a9c9bfc119704de2e67ce360b3eb4b1701f2a21fbeff73ca4d861d" :answer/id #uuid "af3970bc-9d72-5584-b03c-a767f192ddb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5+\\sqrt{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bb6ea7c-3b0b-5a33-9d6c-9a029f7e16d5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274480/field-3/70a2076757a9c9bfc119704de2e67ce360b3eb4b1701f2a21fbeff73ca4d861d" :answer-field/choices ["q-274480/field-3/70a2076757a9c9bfc119704de2e67ce360b3eb4b1701f2a21fbeff73ca4d861d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "904bf4fd-ddba-56d5-bdf1-fcf514fb7c6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "658d3350-05bf-5df7-8277-17ef8c8eac2e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274480/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-274480/field-4/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274480" :question/id #uuid "05ce5300-b428-5c46-807f-7bcb234ad471" :question/math-academy-id "q-274480" :question/problem "From **left to right**, the ellipse $5{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+50x-4y=50$ intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $A$ and $B.$ Find the coordinates of these points.\n\n$A($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,$\n\nand \n\n$\\,B($\n{{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+50x-4y & =50 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+(0)^{2}+50x-4(0) & =50 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+50x & =50 \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x & =10 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+10x+25)-25 & =10 \\\\ (x+5)^{2}-25 & =10 \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =35 \\\\ x+5 & =\\pm \\sqrt{35} \\\\ x & =-5\\pm \\sqrt{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\nA(-5-\\sqrt{35},0)\\,\\text{and}\\,B(-5+\\sqrt{35},0).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274480/field-1" "q-274480/field-2" "q-274480/field-3" "q-274480/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6381faa4-5dfd-58fa-ace7-411fd2a97e98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274480"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328497/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a5515